∇ ok←Run;Passed;Failed;f;raw
 ⍝ Test suite and fixture tooling for the UW Schedule Exporter.
 ⍝
 ⍝ Real Quest pastes can't be committed: they name the student and the instructors.
 ⍝ Committed fixtures are anonymised copies, made with Anonymise:
 ⍝
 ⍝   tests/*.txt             raw pastes. Real names: gitignored, never commit.
 ⍝   tests/fixtures/X.txt    anonymised paste, byte-for-byte the same apart from names
 ⍝   tests/fixtures/X.json   expected parse              } written by the reference
 ⍝   tests/fixtures/X.events expected class meetings     } model, never by uwsch/ical
 ⍝
 ⍝ Expected values never come from the code under test. They come from a separate,
 ⍝ deliberately plain reference model (RefParse, RefEvents), so a bug in uwsch or
 ⍝ ical makes a test fail instead of becoming the expected output. Calendars are
 ⍝ compared by meaning (IcsEvents expands them into meetings), not byte for byte,
 ⍝ and checked separately against RFC 5545 (RfcProblems).
 ⍝
 ⍝ Fixture names come from their content, so the list of names shows what is covered:
 ⍝   <term><year>-<ddmm|mmdd>-<12h|24h>-<lf|crlf|cr>-<plain|tabbed>[-n].txt
 ⍝ (plain/tabbed are the two paste layouts seen so far; tabbed puts a tab-only line
 ⍝ between fields. Which one you get seems to depend on the browser.)
 ⍝
 ⍝ Fixtures are deliberately NOT normalised: odd whitespace and line endings are what
 ⍝ the parser has to cope with. Instead every fixture is also run through regular
 ⍝ variants (see Variants) that must all produce the same calendar.
 ⍝
 ⍝ Usage, from the repository root:
 ⍝   Tests.Run                          run everything; returns 1 if all passed
 ⍝   Tests.Anonymise 'tests/raw.txt'    raw paste → fixture + expected files
 ⍝   Tests.WriteExpected ''             rewrite expected files from the reference model
 ⍝
  Passed←Failed←0
  Say'Unit tests'
  UnitTests
  :If 0=Failed ⋄ Say'  ok (',(⍕Passed),' checks)' ⋄ :EndIf
  Say'Fixtures (',(⍕≢Fixtures),')'
  :For f :In Fixtures
      FixtureTests f
  :EndFor
  :If 0<≢raw←LocalRaw
      Say'Local raw pastes (',(⍕≢raw),', not committed)'
      :For f :In raw
          RawTests f
      :EndFor
  :EndIf
  Say(⍕Passed),' passed, ',(⍕Failed),' failed'
  ok←0=Failed
∇
